<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Merged into the generated iPhone Info.plist by the Tauri CLI, which looks for
  `Info.ios.plist` next to `tauri.conf.json`. Keeping it here rather than
  editing `gen/apple/Yames_iOS/Info.plist` means `ios init` can be re-run
  without losing any of it.

  Two keys, and nothing else on purpose.

  `UIBackgroundModes: audio` is the whole reason the click survives a locked
  screen: without it iOS suspends the app seconds after the screen goes off and
  the metronome on the music stand goes quiet by itself. It is paired with the
  `.playback` audio session in the plugin's Swift half — the entitlement is the
  permission, the session is the use of it.

  Portrait only, per the mobile plan §1. The same lock Android got in M05.

  What is deliberately absent is the more interesting half of the file. There
  is no NSMicrophoneUsageDescription (the mic evaluation does not ship on a
  phone), no camera, no Bluetooth, no local-network and no tracking string.
  The app asks a phone for nothing at all, and `ios.yml` greps the built
  Info.plist and fails if any of those keys ever appears.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
	<array>
		<string>audio</string>
	</array>
	<key>UISupportedInterfaceOrientations</key>
	<array>
		<string>UIInterfaceOrientationPortrait</string>
	</array>
	<key>UISupportedInterfaceOrientations~ipad</key>
	<array>
		<string>UIInterfaceOrientationPortrait</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
